            <ArticleTitle>[Multivessel coronary angioplasty in chronically haemodialysed patient].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>278-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Unstable angina in chronically haemodialysed patients has poor clinical outcome. Surgical treatment of these patients is a procedure of high risk. According to guidelines left main coronary artery stenosis is the indication for by-pass grafting. In some cases the alternative to surgical treatment could become percutaneous coronary intervention. We present the case of the patient in which we have perform multivessel percutaneous coronary angioplasties including left main coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
